-# AutoShield demo recording (about 3 minutes)
-
-Use the deterministic fixture and synthetic DevOps logs. Record only actual results; keep keys and account details off screen.
-
-## Before recording
-
-1. Start the complete stack using README instructions. Verify service health.
-2. Configure scanner and DevOps ArmorIQ policies for their separate agent identities.
-3. In Session, use `http://fixture-lab:8090/`, passive mode, 5 pages, 20 requests, 120 seconds. Confirm authorization. Rehearse an allowed run.
-4. Prepare a second policy configuration that denies the scanner request. Keep all other permissions scoped to the lab. Rehearse the denial separately.
-5. Open the relevant ArmorIQ decision view. Verify it corresponds to the agent/tool and recording run; do not present old events as new.
-
-## Recording sequence
-
-| Time | Show | Explain |
-| --- | --- | --- |
-| 0:00–0:20 | Dashboard and Session readiness | “AutoShield is a policy-enforced assessment workspace. Configuration readiness is separate from a verified policy decision.” |
-| 0:20–1:05 | Start allowed fixture scan; open Activity | “Each target GET travels through MCP and needs an explicit ArmorIQ allow. Scope, DNS, TLS and budgets still apply.” |
-| 1:05–1:30 | One observation and its evidence | “This observation is linked to its response and hash. A missing header is a configuration observation, not proof of exploitation.” |
-| 1:30–2:10 | Enable the prepared deny policy; start a fresh scan | “The denied first request was not executed.” Show the policy outcome, stopped/failed scan and zero target requests. Correlate with ArmorIQ console evidence. |
-| 2:10–2:40 | Export HTML/JSON report | “The result is reviewable evidence. Denied and partial runs retain their history.” |
-| 2:40–3:00 | Limits and architecture | “Selected response checks and two optional query probes; no complete Top 10 or exploit-confirmation claim.” |
-
-Optional: briefly show the separate DevOps MCP lab's injection replay. Label it a scripted proposal using real MCP transport and guard. A local deterministic denial is not a cloud denial. If ArmorIQ mode is disabled, say “local policy only.”
-
-If cloud setup fails, show the failure honestly. Do not substitute a replay or mocked allow and call it live cloud enforcement. AI review is optional and advisory; it cannot execute scan tools.
-
-## Evidence checklist
-
-- Allowed request: actual successful target response and recorded ArmorIQ allow.
-- Denied first request: recorded block, zero target requests, matching console evidence if available.
-- Export: policy outcome, scan limits, findings and coverage limitations.
-- WAF claims, if included: separately demonstrate actual candidate validation and before/after enforcement; scanner output alone does not prove patch deployment.
