-```
+## What the project demonstrates
 
-The DevOps MCP lab is an independent service with fixed command/file/SQL capabilities. `MCP_ARMORIQ_MODE=disabled` is an explicit local-policy-only mode, never scanner bypass or proof of ArmorIQ enforcement. New installations default to `required`.
+- Bounded HTTP(S) crawling with same-origin scope, DNS pinning, public TLS validation and ArmorIQ authorization for every target GET.
+- Evidence-linked observations, two optional query probes, advisory AI review, comparison reports and exports.
+- WAF log finding → trusted proposal → deterministic rule compilation. Candidate validation and explicit promotion are separate steps.
+- MCP capability allowlists, SQL canonicalization, untrusted-log handling and durable ALLOW/BLOCK evidence.
 
-## Evidence and honest coverage
+A reflected marker is not proof of XSS. A database-error signature is not proof of exploitable SQL injection. Coverage is selected OWASP 2021 heuristics, not a complete Top 10 audit. A compiled rule is not a deployed patch. This is a local, single-operator lab.
 
-- Selected OWASP 2021 response heuristics; active mode adds reflection and database-error query probes.
-- Same-origin crawling, DNS address pinning, private/reserved-IP restrictions, public TLS verification, cancellation and bounded requests/time.
-- Saved timelines, policy outcomes, response hashes, JSON/HTML reports and scan comparisons.
-- Repeated header observations are grouped in the React view; per-page findings and IDs remain in exports.
-- A confirmed observation is not confirmed exploitability. Reflection is not proof of XSS; an error signature is not proof of exploitable SQL injection.
-- No browser JavaScript, authenticated crawl, full OWASP Top 10 audit, arbitrary exploitation or multi-tenant authentication.
-- A policy block stops the scan, so findings may be incomplete. No findings does not establish security.
